# .env.local.example — machine-local overrides that should NOT be committed.
#
# Copy to .env.local and edit. The scripts merge it on top of .env, so only
# the keys you actually set here override the committed defaults.
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# .env.local is gitignored.

# --- Model storage (REQUIRED — must be a Windows path on Docker Desktop) -----
# MODELS_DIR=//d/llm-models

# --- GPU tuning -------------------------------------------------------------
# If you have more/less than 24 GB VRAM, adjust context and cache sizes here.
# CTX_SIZE=32768
# CACHE_RAM=4096

# --- Network ----------------------------------------------------------------
# BIND_ADDR=0.0.0.0    # expose on the LAN
# LLAMA_PORT=8080
# FORGE_PORT=8081

# --- pi ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# PI_EXTRA_ARGS=--approve
# PI_CONTEXT_FILES=0     # on by default; 0 passes -nc and skips AGENTS.md
# PI_MAX_TOKENS=8192     # keep LLAMA_EXTRA_FLAGS' -n in step with this

# --- Execution backend / hosted Anthropic mode ------------------------------
# scripts/mode.sh manages STACK_BACKEND and STACK_LAST_LOCAL_MODE in .env.
# STACK_BACKEND=local uses llama.cpp behind forge; STACK_BACKEND=anthropic
# bypasses both containers. STACK_LAST_LOCAL_MODE names the local profile that
# `./scripts/mode.sh local` restores after a hosted session.
#
# Do not override mode keys here unless you intend to pin them for every launch:
# .env.local and exported variables win over .env, and mode.sh refuses a switch
# that cannot make every key in the selected mode file effective.
#
# Hosted defaults live in modes/anthropic.env:
#   ./scripts/mode.sh anthropic  # switch to hosted and refresh pi's provider
#   ./scripts/mode.sh local      # restore STACK_LAST_LOCAL_MODE, no restart
#   ./scripts/mode.sh anthropic --restart llama  # warns; Docker is never used
#
# Set the hosted credential only in this gitignored file. Mode files and .env
# must stay key-free. pi reads the key when the launcher installs the hosted
# provider; relaunch a running pi session after any backend switch.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-key-here

# --- team-solve -------------------------------------------------------------
# Anthropic-mode only. The defaults in .env and modes/anthropic.env route Fable
# to planning/management/audit, Opus to implementation/repair, Sonnet to
# ideation/review, and Haiku to routing/triage. Override model ids or pi effort
# levels here only when a task genuinely needs a different allocation.
# TEAM_SOLVE_ENABLED=1
# TEAM_SOLVE_FABLE_MODEL=claude-fable-5-1
# TEAM_SOLVE_OPUS_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# TEAM_SOLVE_SONNET_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# TEAM_SOLVE_HAIKU_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# TEAM_SOLVE_FABLE_THINKING=high
# TEAM_SOLVE_OPUS_THINKING=high
# TEAM_SOLVE_SONNET_THINKING=high
# TEAM_SOLVE_HAIKU_THINKING=medium
# TEAM_SOLVE_DEFAULT_PROFILE=auto
# TEAM_SOLVE_MAX_ROUNDS=10
# TEAM_SOLVE_MAX_HOURS=72
# TEAM_SOLVE_ROLE_TIMEOUT=4h
# TEAM_SOLVE_CHECK_TIMEOUT=1h
# TEAM_SOLVE_ROLE_RETRIES=1
# TEAM_SOLVE_MULTI_DAY=1

# --- MCP via CLI ------------------------------------------------------------
# MCP2CLI_ENABLED=0     # on by default; set 0 to drop the mcp-tools skill

# --- Matrix channel ---------------------------------------------------------
# Off by default for two reasons: it logs a bot into a homeserver and makes the
# session addressable from the internet, and its six tool schemas cost ~1,470
# tokens of every request. Setting it here makes it permanent for this machine;
# prefer the one-launch form below if you only occasionally want Matrix.
# PRINNY_ENABLED=1

# --- persona -----------------------------------------------------------------
# /persona is on by default and costs nothing until a persona is active. Once
# one is, it is ~3,683 tokens of every request (~2,311 on `lean`) against a
# 32,768-token window — /persona status prints the live number.
# PERSONA_ENABLED=0        # drop /persona entirely
# PERSONA_PROMPT_MODE=lean # the same contract, ~1,372 tokens cheaper
# PERSONA_IMMERSION=off       # first-message thinking-mode marker; ON by default
#
# chub.ai gateway key. OPTIONAL — the extension sends no key when this is unset,
# and both gateway routes were measured answering 200 without one. Set it here
# (this file is gitignored) and never in .env, which is tracked.
# CHUB_API_KEY=your-key-here
#
# DeepSeek key for orchestrator mode (ORCHESTRATOR=1 in .env). Required only
# there; pi's built-in deepseek provider reads it from the environment, and the
# launcher never writes it into models.json. For pi in a container, put it in
# the CONTAINER checkout's .env.local — that is the file its launcher reads.
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=your-key-here

# --- pi in a container (optional) --------------------------------------------
# Set this and ./scripts/pi-container.sh works; leave it empty and it refuses
# rather than guessing. It is the agent home AS THE DOCKER DAEMON SEES IT — on
# Docker Desktop, docker's form of the Windows path, never a WSL path.
# PI_CONTAINER_HOME_HOST=//c/path/to/pi-home
# PI_CONTAINER_EXTRA_ARGS=-v //c/path/to/scratch:/home/piuser/scratch
# Ovis access token; unset, one is generated into ~/.config/ovis/token in the
# container home. Put it in the CONTAINER checkout's .env.local.
# OVIS_TOKEN=a-long-random-string
# OVIS_TOKEN=off      # no sign-in; see docs/container.md before using it

# --- pi updates -------------------------------------------------------------
# PI_AUTO_UPDATE=0        # pin the installed pi instead of tracking npm latest
# PI_UPDATE_INTERVAL_H=72 # check less often

# Any key here can also be set for ONE launch, without editing a file:
#   PI_CONTEXT_FILES=1 ./scripts/pi-local.sh

